        "Content": "SPACIOUS COUNTRY LIVING ON APPROX. 0.8 ACRES – STABLES – GARAGE/WORKSHOP – EXTENSIVE GROUNDS\r\n\r\nFLEENSTOWN, THE WARD, CO. MEATH, D11 Y891\r\n\r\nSet in the countryside at Fleenstown, The Ward, this substantial three-bedroom property offers a wonderful combination of spacious living accommodation and country life, all set on approximately 0.8 acres of grounds.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 1986 and extending to approximately 192m², the property provides generous and versatile accommodation throughout. Outside, the property is approached via a large wrap-around driveway with ample off-street parking and benefits from an impressive range of additional features including horse stables, garage/workshop, greenhouse, aviary, duck and fish ponds, decking and patio areas.\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE:\r\n•\tSet on approximately 0.8 acres of grounds. \r\n•\tLarge wrap-around driveway with ample off-street parking. \r\n•\tExtensive gardens and outdoor space. \r\n•\tHorse stables. \r\n•\tGarage/workshop offering excellent additional storage or workspace. \r\n•\tGreenhouse. \r\n•\tAviary. \r\n•\tDuck ponds and fish ponds. \r\n•\tDecking area with ample space for outdoor seating and entertaining. \r\n•\tSeparate patio area. \r\n•      Potential to convert granny flat as there is a second entrance and kitchen. \r\n•      Fresh water well on property grounds for horses\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION:\r\n•\tEntrance Hall (4.16m x 11.73m) Hardwood flooring, dado rails, ribboned coving and security alarm system. \r\n•\tLiving Room (3.62m x 4.87m) Hardwood flooring, large double-glazed windows, wood-burning multi-stove, wall panelling, coving and TV/internet points. \r\n•\tKitchen/Lounge (8.31m x 3.62m) Generously proportioned open-plan space with hardwood flooring, double-glazed windows, radiators and TV points. Fully tiled kitchen area with shaker-style cabinetry, gas hob and plumbing for washing machine. \r\n•\tSunroom (2.85m x 3.91m) Bright additional living space overlooking the grounds. \r\n•\tShower Room (2.07m x 1.35m) Fitted with telephone-style shower. \r\n•\tGuest W/C (2.09m x 0.85m) Wash-hand basin and toilet. \r\n•\tBedroom 1 (3.03m x 4.66m) Hardwood flooring, radiator, TV point, ceiling fan, built-in wardrobes and large windows. \r\n•\tBedroom 2 (3.62m x 4.68m) Carpet flooring, radiators, built-in wardrobes, ribboned coving and large window. \r\n•\tBedroom 3 (5.10m x 3.82m) Laminate flooring, built-in wardrobes, ribboned coving and large window. \r\n•\tMain Bathroom (3.03m x 2.51m) Three-piece pink bathroom suite, Triton T90SR electric shower, tiled flooring and half-tiled walls.\r\n•\tSecondary Kitchen/Dining Room (3.01m x 4.40m) Hardwood flooring with tiled kitchen area and gas hob, providing additional flexible living and dining accommodation. \r\n•\tSecondary Sunroom (2.22m x 3.69m) Bright and versatile additional living space. \r\n\r\nATTIC/LOFT:\r\n•\tAttic/Loft (3.37m x 5.17m) Accessed via hot press/storage room, insulated with wooden flooring, alcove storage and two skylights, providing excellent additional storage space. \r\n\r\nPROPERTY DETAILS:\r\nOverall Size: Approx. 192m²\r\nSite Size: Approx. 0.8 acres\r\nBER: C3\r\nBER No.: 105283238\r\nHeating: Oil Fired Central Heating\r\nYear Built: 1986\r\n\r\nThe grounds are a particular feature of this property and offer excellent versatility for those with equestrian interests, gardening enthusiasts or buyers seeking additional outdoor space. The combination of horse stables, garage/workshop, greenhouse, aviary, ponds and dedicated decking and patio areas provides an excellent opportunity to enjoy country living while remaining within convenient reach of surrounding towns and Dublin.\r\n\r\nLOCATION & TRANSPORT:\r\nFleenstown enjoys a peaceful countryside setting while remaining within easy reach of Ashbourne and Ratoath, both of which offer an excellent range of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and everyday amenities.\r\nThe property is well positioned for commuters, with the R125 just a couple of minutes away and convenient access to the N2/M2, M3 and M50 road networks. Dublin Airport and the M50 are approximately a 20-minute drive away, providing excellent connectivity to Dublin City and the wider motorway network.\r\n\r\nPublic transport options are also available nearby, with bus stops approximately 1.8–2.1km away offering services towards Ashbourne, Ratoath and Dublin. M3 Parkway Railway Station is approximately 6.7km away, providing further commuter connections.\r\n\r\nViewing by appointment only. Details, photos, sizes and distances are for guidance purposes only."
      },
